1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:02,210
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,940
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,750
(Episode 27)

4
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:09,210
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

5
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,580
Wait. This is where I was earlier.

6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,050
And Dr. Ju's clinic
is right over here.

7
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:17,220
It is.

8
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:22,730
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

9
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:43,050
You really came.

10
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,180
- I am sorry. Am I late?
- No, not at all.

11
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:47,850
How did you find this...

12
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,190
- May I sit down first?
- Yes, please. Have a seat.

13
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:05,870
This is my mom's place.

14
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:08,470
Your mother's?

15
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:12,210
Yes. She took it over
from my grandma.

16
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,380
I grew up here too.

17
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:17,150
I heard you quit
the department store...

18
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:18,750
Are you drinking
because you are upset?

19
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:23,920
Yes. I just felt like
having a drink today.

20
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:26,190
Then please pour me a glass too.

21
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:31,830
Did you not drive here?
If you are doing this to comfort me,

22
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:33,970
I appreciate the thought,
but that is plenty.

23
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:37,540
Besides, I was about to wrap up
and head out after this.

24
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:40,310
All right, let us do that then.

25
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:42,710
But I do not drive.

26
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:44,340
I do not even own a car.

27
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:47,510
Really? I assumed
you would have one.

28
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,620
I am not particularly fond
of riding in cars.

29
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:53,180
Well, when I have no choice,
I take a taxi sometimes.

30
00:01:54,390 --> 00:01:55,490
That is surprising.

31
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:57,890
These days, it feels like...

32
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:59,290
everyone drives
as a matter of course.

33
00:02:01,490 --> 00:02:03,730
By the way, what was it
you wanted to give me?

34
00:02:04,330 --> 00:02:06,030
Here.

35
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:08,330
What is this?

36
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:10,440
Open it.

37
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,140
Wait...

38
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,450
(The Second Sketch
Is More You, Da Mi.)

39
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:24,380
When did you write all of this down?

40
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:29,120
I saw it the day my sister...

41
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,190
swapped tablets with you by mistake,

42
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,590
and I have looked at it
whenever I had time since.

43
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:35,890
My goodness.

44
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:38,060
You really did not have to...

45
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
To get such detailed feedback...

46
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,470
from a world-famous designer...

47
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,840
I never do anything
I find uninteresting.

48
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,480
Pardon?

49
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:56,210
I did it because I enjoyed it,

50
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,750
so do not read too much into it.
That is all I mean.

51
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:04,160
(For This Design...
100% Cotton Over Linen)

52
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,930
I hope it helps you, Da Mi.

53
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,670
Since I already handed it over.

54
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:17,600
It is more than just helpful.

55
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:22,040
I was feeling so down
and exhausted all day,

56
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:25,080
but seeing this
makes me feel so much better.

57
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:27,910
Thank you so much.

58
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:33,380
I am glad to know
it was not a waste of time.

59
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:37,360
Did you really quit
the department store, though?

60
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,720
Yes.

61
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:43,960
Why?

62
00:03:46,130 --> 00:03:47,830
If I had not quit,

63
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:51,300
one of my coworkers
would have lost her job.

64
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:55,070
Her father is currently very sick.

65
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:57,540
She told me that
if she lost her job,

66
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:01,180
she had no idea how she would pay
for his hospital bills next month.

67
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:03,210
So...

68
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:07,520
Wait, are you
saying that you quit...

69
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:09,720
just to take the fall
for your coworker, Da Mi?

70
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:11,960
I was her manager.

71
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:16,890
Her making a mistake means
I failed to look after her properly.

72
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:20,330
Still, making that kind
of decision alone...

73
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:21,470
could not have been easy.

74
00:04:21,770 --> 00:04:22,800
You know what?

75
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:27,210
When the rich cough,

76
00:04:27,610 --> 00:04:29,940
people like us get blown over.

77
00:04:30,810 --> 00:04:31,980
And we fall hard.

78
00:04:35,450 --> 00:04:37,920
They make an offhand remark...

79
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,480
say they will never shop
at our store again,

80
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:40,650
and that is that.

81
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:44,690
Then we have to figure out
who was at fault,

82
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,990
and someone has to take the blame.

83
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,300
Then what do you plan to do now?

84
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:57,100
I am not sure.
I need some time to think it over.

85
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:03,440
Still, not knowing
what kind of person I am...

86
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:04,940
or what I can do
made today so much harder.

87
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:09,450
Still, I do not think
it is entirely over.

88
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,190
It is not over. It is just a pause.

89
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,720
As long as you
do not give up on yourself, that is.

90
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:23,360
I should get going now.
Please, do not bother seeing me out.

91
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,960
Have a safe trip home.

92
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,280
(Wool Felted Suit Outfit,
Diagonal Style)

93
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,480
(Linear Texture for Confident,
Smart Career Look)

94
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:44,380
I did not know
he had this side to him.

95
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:47,450
That is really unexpected.

96
00:06:13,410 --> 00:06:15,210
- Da Mi.
- Yes?

97
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,280
Are you sick?

98
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:19,780
No.

99
00:06:20,990 --> 00:06:23,090
Then why are you
just picking at your food?

100
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:26,190
You have looked awful
since yesterday,

101
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:28,290
and you came home early
from the store, too.

102
00:06:30,130 --> 00:06:31,430
Did something happen?

103
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:35,230
I am just really tired, that is all.
Nothing happened.

104
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,370
What do you mean, nothing?

105
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,370
You know you cannot lie
to your mother, right?

106
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:43,140
I can tell just by the way
you avoid my eyes.

107
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:47,980
Mom.

108
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,450
- And Grandma.
- Yes?

109
00:06:52,050 --> 00:06:54,590
I quit my job
at the department store.

110
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:57,460
What?

111
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,720
You quit your job?

112
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:01,830
Look at you.

113
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:04,030
Did you really quit?

114
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,430
Yes.

115
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:10,330
Why on earth would you quit
a perfectly good job out of nowhere?

116
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:14,410
I guess I just got burned out
after working there for so long.

117
00:07:14,470 --> 00:07:15,710
It was getting hard
to hang in there.

118
00:07:15,910 --> 00:07:17,410
What kind of nonsense is that?

119
00:07:18,210 --> 00:07:19,580
You quit just because you are tired?

120
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:21,150
Mom.

121
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:24,080
Did I say something wrong?

122
00:07:24,850 --> 00:07:27,050
How could you leave
such a good job out of nowhere?

123
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:29,890
It was not out of nowhere.

124
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:33,090
Then what was it?
You have elders in this house,

125
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,390
so how could you just resign
on a whim...

126
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:35,790
without discussing it first?

127
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,530
Is it enough to drop the news
like this?

128
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:40,130
I am an adult.

129
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,500
A grown-up.

130
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:43,670
I was having a really hard time,

131
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,570
and I thought it over
before handing in my resignation.

132
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,740
I wanted to rest.

133
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:49,210
I haven't taken a single break
from work...

134
00:07:49,310 --> 00:07:50,540
ever since I graduated from college.

135
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:52,210
If you needed rest,

136
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,080
you could have used up all
your unused vacation days.

137
00:07:55,910 --> 00:07:58,380
Knowing full well how
things are at home,

138
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:00,120
how could you just throw
away your job like that?

139
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:01,750
What are you thinking?

140
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,190
Do I have to live my life
constantly worrying...

141
00:08:04,290 --> 00:08:05,360
about my brothers' situations?

142
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:08,760
I'll take care of my own business,
so don't worry about me.

143
00:08:10,430 --> 00:08:11,430
I'm sorry, Grandma.

144
00:08:12,030 --> 00:08:13,030
Please excuse me.

145
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,200
All right.

146
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,070
"Take care of it?"

147
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,940
Do you know how hard you worked
to get into that company?

148
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,840
Does everyone just quit
whenever their job gets tough?

149
00:08:25,310 --> 00:08:27,180
Stop it, Mom.

150
00:08:27,410 --> 00:08:29,450
She said she endured it
as long as she could.

151
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:30,620
You be quiet.

152
00:08:33,350 --> 00:08:34,350
So immature.

153
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,760
How does she plan to live
without a paycheck?

154
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,290
Did she think the world
would just bend...

155
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,460
to her every whim?

156
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:46,200
Well, she was at that company
for a very long time.

157
00:08:46,330 --> 00:08:49,530
If she had just talked to me first,
I wouldn't be this upset, Mother.

158
00:08:50,170 --> 00:08:53,940
Every single one of my children...

159
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,310
(The second sketch
is more you, Da Mi.)

160
00:09:02,410 --> 00:09:04,620
The second sketch
is more you, Da Mi.

161
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,460
Let's go.

162
00:09:18,730 --> 00:09:19,730
Dad.

163
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:23,630
- Yes, sweetheart?
- Did Aunt Da Mi go broke like you?

164
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:31,510
She said she quit
because it was too hard.

165
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:32,910
She's not broke.

166
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,950
But Grandma is mad.

167
00:09:35,210 --> 00:09:36,850
Grandma is...

168
00:09:37,450 --> 00:09:39,320
She's just worried about your aunt.

169
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:42,990
Mom was always worried
about you too.

170
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,860
- Listen, sweetheart.
- Yes?

171
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:52,000
I'm definitely not completely broke.

172
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:53,830
But Mom said so.

173
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:57,770
She said you were completely,
totally ruined this time.

174
00:10:01,870 --> 00:10:02,970
Well...

175
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:07,040
Mom was just worrying about me
way too much,

176
00:10:07,450 --> 00:10:09,880
so she got upset and misspoke.
That's all.

177
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:14,020
And Su Ah, Kang Su Ah.

178
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:20,120
Even if the whole world says that,
you have to believe in your dad.

179
00:10:20,890 --> 00:10:23,190
- Why?
- Because...

180
00:10:23,590 --> 00:10:26,330
As long as you believe in me
and cheer me on,

181
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,700
I think I will find
the strength to endure it.

182
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Really.

183
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,500
Could you do that for me?

184
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,610
Please, okay?

185
00:10:37,510 --> 00:10:38,510
Okay.

186
00:10:40,810 --> 00:10:42,550
I knew I could count on you.

187
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:45,850
I sure made one amazing daughter.

188
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:49,220
Hang in there, Dad.

189
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:51,760
Yes, I will hang in there.

190
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:06,700
Even that Da Mi girl is giving you
such a terrible headache.

191
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:10,510
I just knew this would happen.
I knew that one day...

192
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:13,440
she was going to stab you
right in the back.

193
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,790
What is it?
Does your chest feel tight?

194
00:11:23,650 --> 00:11:24,660
It's just...

195
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:27,790
I feel so suffocated.

196
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:29,660
This is bad.

197
00:11:30,930 --> 00:11:34,500
Let us go see Dr. Ju together.

198
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:37,640
You are going to collapse next
because of your kids.

199
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:40,270
It's just around the corner.
Why go together?

200
00:11:41,210 --> 00:11:42,210
Watch the restaurant.

201
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,340
If it gets too bad,
I can go by myself.

202
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:48,210
Well, that is true, but...

203
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:50,150
Having the clinic so close...

204
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:51,550
is actually a problem
at times like this.

205
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:55,050
Are you two planning
to close up shop today?

206
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:57,820
I'm coming, Mother.

207
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:00,220
Well, Mi Mi...

208
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,990
She isn't feeling well at all,
Mrs. Choi.

209
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:04,060
How bad is it?

210
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,730
- Bad enough to be laid up in bed?
- No, Mother.

211
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:11,070
I just have a bit of a headache.

212
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:13,400
I took some medicine,
so I will be fine.

213
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:15,310
- What?
- Let us go.

214
00:12:29,390 --> 00:12:30,390
Right...

215
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,420
Oh, Mother.

216
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,020
Yes?

217
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:36,690
The side dishes
and kimchi in the fridge...

218
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:38,730
Did you happen
to give them to someone?

219
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,400
Why are you asking that?

220
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:44,900
While making breakfast,

221
00:12:45,170 --> 00:12:47,840
I noticed the side dishes and kimchi
were mostly gone.

222
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:51,540
The containers and wrapping cloth
were missing too,

223
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,410
so I figured you must have
given them to someone.

224
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:56,210
Did you not?

225
00:12:56,950 --> 00:12:59,350
Well, you know.

226
00:12:59,850 --> 00:13:03,650
There's that elderly Mrs. Oh
who lives alone in the neighborhood.

227
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:05,590
I gave them to her.

228
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:09,460
- Mrs. Oh?
- Yes.

229
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:10,900
She lives alone and said...

230
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:13,030
making side dishes
was too much trouble,

231
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:14,930
so I brought her a little bit.

232
00:13:16,530 --> 00:13:19,740
Well, next time, Mother,
please be sure to tell me first.

233
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:25,410
Do I need to ask for your permission
just to give away a few side dishes?

234
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:30,880
That's not what I meant.
I just found it so strange...

235
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,950
that I spent a while looking
everywhere, so I...

236
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:37,390
You did a good deed, Mrs. Choi.

237
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:39,760
Mi Mi, let us hurry
to the restaurant.

238
00:13:40,190 --> 00:13:41,460
It will get busy
welcoming customers...

239
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:42,530
Come on, let us go.

240
00:13:42,590 --> 00:13:47,000
Yes, Mother, we will head out first.
Take your time coming out.

241
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:48,870
Let us go.

242
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,850
I even used Mrs. Oh as an excuse.

243
00:14:03,110 --> 00:14:07,080
Now I must keep up that lie awhile.

244
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:09,920
Wait.

245
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:12,490
Those reishi mushrooms...

246
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,930
that Mi Seon brought
looked pretty good.

247
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:19,630
No, no.

248
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,400
What is wrong with me?

249
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,970
I cannot even control myself.

250
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:31,080
Where did your common sense go,
Soon Deok?

251
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:32,610
Goodness.

252
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:39,920
You are making such a huge fuss.

253
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:42,220
Honey.

254
00:14:44,390 --> 00:14:45,690
Do not take my words lightly.

255
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,560
- What words?
- If you let your mother...

256
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:53,700
set foot in my house one more time,
I told you I would divorce you too.

257
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:55,130
Divorce?

258
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:56,770
Divorce?

259
00:14:57,530 --> 00:14:58,700
Did you really just say that?

260
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:00,300
Look here, Park Ji Young.

261
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:03,170
How can you bring up divorce
so carelessly?

262
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:07,280
Well, then do you
want Ye Ri to know...

263
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:08,610
what a dysfunctional mess
your family is?

264
00:15:08,710 --> 00:15:11,150
- Why is my family a mess?
- You really have to ask?

265
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:13,480
Ye Ri caught the eye
of the company CEO,

266
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:15,690
and she is just waiting
to marry into that family...

267
00:15:15,750 --> 00:15:19,060
- and if your family is like that...
- Hey, who made it a mess?

268
00:15:19,590 --> 00:15:21,390
You and I did this.

269
00:15:21,830 --> 00:15:25,030
Who crushed a perfectly good family
to pieces?

270
00:15:25,230 --> 00:15:26,230
Did you forget?

271
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:30,030
Who said I forgot?

272
00:15:30,870 --> 00:15:33,940
For the sake of our Ye Ri's future,
I am saying you must make sure...

273
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:36,110
your mother never comes
to our house again.

274
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,710
I know very well what I did,
so stop badgering me about it.

275
00:15:41,810 --> 00:15:44,150
Let us go make money now.

276
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:51,320
She is certainly quick to admit it.

277
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:54,790
That is why I can never
completely hate her.

278
00:15:55,030 --> 00:15:56,060
Gosh.

279
00:15:56,630 --> 00:15:59,230
Right, let us go make money.

280
00:16:05,770 --> 00:16:09,170
Well, Mother.
She needs to head to work,

281
00:16:09,470 --> 00:16:10,670
so could you please...

282
00:16:15,210 --> 00:16:16,280
Jin Hee.

283
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:17,850
Yes, Mother.

284
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:21,420
Yesterday was the anniversary
of Jun Sung and his wife's passing,

285
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:24,290
so I let it slide quietly,

286
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,360
but I must address it today.

287
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:29,830
Please go ahead.

288
00:16:30,230 --> 00:16:33,800
I must have done something
to displease you.

289
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:37,870
I felt so bitter toward my late son
and daughter-in-law...

290
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:42,070
that all this time, I never
looked into the living room...

291
00:16:43,110 --> 00:16:45,740
where you set up the memorial table
or bowed, did I?

292
00:16:46,610 --> 00:16:48,110
And then...

293
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:51,720
Yesterday, Seung Yun,
the eldest grandson,

294
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:55,450
led his parents' memorial service
for the first time,

295
00:16:55,990 --> 00:17:00,590
- so I watched the whole thing.
- Come on, Mother.

296
00:17:01,190 --> 00:17:04,500
She worked so hard all these years
for their memorial services.

297
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,230
You know that too.

298
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:09,270
Who said she didn't?

299
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:11,170
Even yesterday...

300
00:17:12,170 --> 00:17:15,140
I told your wife
she worked hard, didn't I?

301
00:17:16,310 --> 00:17:18,110
Then what...

302
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,480
Jin Hee.

303
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:22,380
You went through so much trouble...

304
00:17:23,110 --> 00:17:25,420
setting the table
with store-bought food,

305
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,190
pretending you made it all yourself.

306
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,890
Mother, how did you...

307
00:17:33,490 --> 00:17:36,830
What, did you think I was blind?
Did you?

308
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:39,130
Every single year,

309
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:42,130
I checked the security footage
outside the gate.

310
00:17:43,630 --> 00:17:46,340
I saw you carrying
in all that food...

311
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,840
you bought with your money.

312
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:52,810
I am so sorry, Mother.

313
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:58,350
I will not make any excuses.
I was completely in the wrong.

314
00:17:59,050 --> 00:18:02,150
Then the food
on the table yesterday...

315
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:07,060
We served food Mrs. Anseong
shopped for and prepared.

316
00:18:07,890 --> 00:18:10,860
I instructed her beforehand,
just in case.

317
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:13,430
Do Yun's father.

318
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,300
Yes, Mother.

319
00:18:15,870 --> 00:18:19,940
You must understand
that you are largely to blame...

320
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:22,540
for your wife's conduct.

321
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:24,680
Husband and wife
are of one body and mind.

322
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:28,080
If she had just made
the memorial food by hand this time,

323
00:18:28,650 --> 00:18:31,920
I was going to reinstate you as CEO.

324
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:37,290
I am disappointed in both of you.

325
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:41,730
Leave.

326
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:44,290
I am sorry.

327
00:18:53,770 --> 00:18:55,110
Honey, are you okay?

328
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,410
Slowly, be careful.

329
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:14,930
I am fine.

330
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:21,700
I told you not to fuss over me
in front of Mother.

331
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:25,240
My body just moves on its own.
What can I do?

332
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:28,110
Besides, if I do not
look out for you, who will?

333
00:19:29,570 --> 00:19:31,510
I am sorry.
This is all because of me.

334
00:19:32,910 --> 00:19:35,180
And about the memorial food...

335
00:19:35,710 --> 00:19:38,750
I understand you.

336
00:19:40,050 --> 00:19:41,050
Really?

337
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:42,690
Even with work at the company alone,

338
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,920
you are swamped beyond belief.

339
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:46,960
On top of that,
you look after Mother,

340
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:49,130
the kids, and me.

341
00:19:49,490 --> 00:19:51,560
Even 24 hours a day
is not enough for you.

342
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:53,560
I already thought it was too much...

343
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:54,700
for you to make
all the memorial food...

344
00:19:54,870 --> 00:19:56,830
from scratch yourself.

345
00:19:58,770 --> 00:19:59,800
Thank you.

346
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:03,710
Of course. It is only natural.
Hurry and head to work.

347
00:20:15,090 --> 00:20:16,390
Mom is leaving late for work.

348
00:20:17,490 --> 00:20:18,560
Where are your brothers?

349
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:21,090
They knew Grandma
had summoned Mom to her room,

350
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,630
so both slipped out to work.

351
00:20:23,230 --> 00:20:25,260
The memorial service
went well yesterday.

352
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:26,660
Why is Grandma
acting like that again?

353
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:28,600
Did she say something to Mom again?

354
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:31,270
A little.

355
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,370
Grandma is being so unfair.

356
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:38,980
(Low Bun Style)

357
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:41,210
(Clear Length Differences
Between Layers)

358
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,860
Hello, this is Manager Kang Da Mi...

359
00:20:57,290 --> 00:20:59,330
This is Kang Da Mi.

360
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:04,530
Yes.
Could I see you for a moment today?

361
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:19,280
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

362
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:22,090
- Hello.
- Have you been waiting long?

363
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:23,720
No, I just got here.

364
00:21:24,690 --> 00:21:27,120
The sky looked so pretty,
so I was watching it.

365
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:33,000
Since you came by,
you could have come in.

366
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,430
Why did you ask to meet here?

367
00:21:34,930 --> 00:21:36,800
The coffee in our company lounge
is pretty good.

368
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,740
After working cooped up
in a store for years,

369
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:43,310
getting some fresh air
feels better to me.

370
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:46,840
Thank you for coming out.

371
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:50,910
Convenience store coffee
is not too bad either.

372
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:54,720
Thank you. I will enjoy it.

373
00:21:55,850 --> 00:21:57,150
Did you not get anything
for yourself, Da Mi?

374
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:59,320
I do not handle coffee very well,

375
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:02,060
so I brought water.

376
00:22:04,160 --> 00:22:05,160
Honestly,

377
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:08,170
I thought it would take a few days
for you to think it over,

378
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:10,030
so I was surprised when you asked
to meet right away.

379
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:12,400
My mind was already made up,

380
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:15,110
so I thought it would be better
to tell you as soon as possible.

381
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,740
I hope it is good news.

382
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:23,450
I truly appreciate
such a wonderful offer,

383
00:22:24,550 --> 00:22:26,350
but I will respectfully decline.

384
00:22:31,090 --> 00:22:33,960
I thought it was
a decent offer for you, Da Mi.

385
00:22:34,830 --> 00:22:36,430
I genuinely meant it...

386
00:22:36,630 --> 00:22:37,690
when I said
it was a wonderful offer.

387
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,600
May I ask why
you are turning it down?

388
00:22:42,700 --> 00:22:43,870
To be honest?

389
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:47,500
Yes, I would appreciate
your honesty.

390
00:22:51,210 --> 00:22:54,210
Accepting your offer,
Team Leader Cha,

391
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:57,480
means that I would have to work
at Hwanggeum Apparel,

392
00:22:59,380 --> 00:23:01,820
and I just do not want to work
at Hwanggeum Apparel.

393
00:23:03,290 --> 00:23:04,720
That is all.

394
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:10,030
Why do you not want to work at...

395
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:15,700
I do not have any good memories
associated with Hwanggeum Apparel.

396
00:23:17,570 --> 00:23:19,300
I will leave it at that.

397
00:23:19,870 --> 00:23:20,870
I would appreciate it...

398
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:22,910
if you did not ask
for any more details.

399
00:23:25,210 --> 00:23:26,280
I understand.

400
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:30,910
I will get going now.

401
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:32,680
Wait...

402
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:35,350
Does this mean...

403
00:23:35,890 --> 00:23:37,390
we will not be seeing
each other anymore?

404
00:23:38,590 --> 00:23:40,090
I suppose so.

405
00:23:41,730 --> 00:23:43,230
Take care, Team Leader Cha.

406
00:24:01,010 --> 00:24:02,450
Is it because of that complaint?

407
00:24:04,410 --> 00:24:06,920
If that is really the reason
she quit the department store...

408
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:22,400
Kang Da Mi is definitely that girl
from the department store.

409
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:25,570
Why would Team Leader Cha
be so happy to get her call...

410
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:27,200
and rush outside like that?

411
00:24:28,970 --> 00:24:30,010
What could they be talking about...

412
00:24:30,070 --> 00:24:31,710
that's taking him this long
to come back?

413
00:24:36,310 --> 00:24:38,220
- Where are you going?
- Well...

414
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:41,350
You rushed out
after taking that call...

415
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:42,620
Did you manage...

416
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,850
to take care of everything,
Team Leader Cha?

417
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:48,060
Well, things didn't go so well,
in the end.

418
00:24:48,430 --> 00:24:50,760
Really? That is too bad.

419
00:24:51,030 --> 00:24:52,960
Though I don't really know
what happened.

420
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,700
I was going to share the news...

421
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:56,630
if things went well,
so it's a shame.

422
00:24:57,500 --> 00:25:00,100
Assistant Manager Kang,
you haven't been introduced...

423
00:25:00,170 --> 00:25:01,640
to Designer Jaden Cha yet, right?

424
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:03,070
No, I haven't.

425
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:06,080
I'll introduce you.
Let's go say hello.

426
00:25:06,440 --> 00:25:07,480
Yes, Team Leader Cha.

427
00:25:09,580 --> 00:25:11,410
(Product Planning)

428
00:25:24,730 --> 00:25:27,700
Even with the assistant designers
downstairs,

429
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:30,900
there's so much work piling up
in my office right now.

430
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,700
I need to find a solution.

431
00:25:36,270 --> 00:25:37,570
Excuse us for a moment.

432
00:25:44,350 --> 00:25:46,450
Hello, Designer Jaden Cha.

433
00:25:47,050 --> 00:25:50,220
I'm Assistant Manager Kang Ye Ri
from Product Planning,

434
00:25:50,290 --> 00:25:51,550
working alongside
Team Leader Cha Do Yun.

435
00:25:52,890 --> 00:25:54,060
Hello. Nice to meet you.

436
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:55,990
You certainly seem
full of confidence.

437
00:25:56,090 --> 00:25:57,360
Yes, nice to meet you too.

438
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:01,230
You didn't even give me
a chance to introduce you.

439
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:03,530
Well, introductions are done anyway.

440
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:07,940
By the way, you mentioned
looking for someone...

441
00:26:07,970 --> 00:26:09,810
to run the pop-up store.
How did that go?

442
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:13,940
I found the perfect person
and actively courted her,

443
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:16,010
but I got flat-out rejected.

444
00:26:17,010 --> 00:26:18,010
Courted her?

445
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:20,220
You know her too,
Assistant Manager Kang.

446
00:26:20,650 --> 00:26:23,390
It's Kang Da Mi,
the department store's VIP manager.

447
00:26:23,690 --> 00:26:26,660
Her? I mean, you offered a job...

448
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:28,490
to that employee, Team Leader Cha?

449
00:26:30,190 --> 00:26:31,490
Why shouldn't I?

450
00:26:32,460 --> 00:26:35,270
She was the one who gave me the idea
for launching the sneakers.

451
00:26:36,070 --> 00:26:39,400
I wanted to bring her here,
but I failed.

452
00:26:40,170 --> 00:26:41,840
I heard she quit
the department store.

453
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,310
Why did she turn you down?

454
00:26:44,370 --> 00:26:45,480
How do you...

455
00:26:46,180 --> 00:26:49,150
I mean, how do you know that,
Designer Cha?

456
00:26:49,550 --> 00:26:51,750
We happened to get acquainted.

457
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:53,220
So why did she turn you down?

458
00:26:55,050 --> 00:26:56,050
I suspect it has something to do...

459
00:26:56,120 --> 00:26:57,450
with the broken heel incident...

460
00:26:57,520 --> 00:26:58,820
when Assistant Manager Kang
complained...

461
00:26:58,890 --> 00:27:01,960
with the department store
on behalf of the CEO.

462
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:03,360
No way.

463
00:27:04,030 --> 00:27:05,430
Are you saying that employee...

464
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:07,630
got fired from the department store
because of me?

465
00:27:09,130 --> 00:27:12,300
She wasn't fired.
I heard she resigned on her own.

466
00:27:13,170 --> 00:27:15,370
Of course, that reason
is just my guess.

467
00:27:17,010 --> 00:27:18,010
Is that so?

468
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:24,980
Then what do you plan to do now?

469
00:27:25,050 --> 00:27:26,850
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

470
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:29,890
I am not sure.
I need some time to think it over.

471
00:27:31,920 --> 00:27:34,360
Still, not knowing
what kind of person I am...

472
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:37,730
or what I can do
made today so much harder.

473
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:42,170
Still, I do not think
it is entirely over.

474
00:27:43,830 --> 00:27:44,830
Designer Cha?

475
00:27:45,770 --> 00:27:46,770
Yes?

476
00:27:46,940 --> 00:27:48,240
What are you thinking so hard about?

477
00:27:49,110 --> 00:27:50,670
Nothing, just an amusing thought.

478
00:28:06,420 --> 00:28:08,320
(Mission: Mompossible)

479
00:28:08,690 --> 00:28:10,230
Mom, please, just this once.

480
00:28:10,530 --> 00:28:13,330
- I do not have any money.
- Is Dae Chi your only child?

481
00:28:13,500 --> 00:28:16,570
- Why do you only help him?
- What could have happened...

482
00:28:16,630 --> 00:28:19,640
to make you quit a steady, great job
with a dependable paycheck?

483
00:28:19,770 --> 00:28:21,940
I am a mother.
How could I not worry?

484
00:28:22,110 --> 00:28:25,580
Did you look into the people
around Do Yun's mother?

485
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:28,410
Are you saying her past
is a total blank?

486
00:28:29,580 --> 00:28:31,580
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
